From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 16:24:33 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc3: drd: Let the role switch wait for a role change

dwc3_usb_role_switch_set() returns as soon as the role is recorded; the
work that dwc3_set_mode() queues changes it. A holder of the role switch
(usb_role_switch_hold()) has to know when the role it asked for is in
effect, for example that the host is gone before it changes what the
port is connected to. The role the switch reports does not tell: it is
the role before until the work gets to it, and a work that is under way
for an earlier request finishes that one first.

Provide the role switch's sync callback, which waits for the work. The
work is queued again by every request, so the wait covers the role asked
for last.

Assisted-by: Claude Fable 5.2
Signed-off-by: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/usb/dwc3/drd.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc3/drd.c b/drivers/usb/dwc3/drd.c
index f3e37d383..68d8c7ae2 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/drd.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/drd.c
@@ -501,6 +501,18 @@ static enum usb_role dwc3_usb_role_switch_get(struct usb_role_switch *sw)
 	return role;
 }
 
+/*
+ * The role is changed by the work that dwc3_set_mode() queues. The work is on
+ * a freezable workqueue, so this must not be called while tasks are frozen
+ * for system sleep.
+ */
+static void dwc3_usb_role_switch_sync(struct usb_role_switch *sw)
+{
+	struct dwc3 *dwc = usb_role_switch_get_drvdata(sw);
+
+	flush_work(&dwc->drd_work);
+}
+
 static int dwc3_setup_role_switch(struct dwc3 *dwc)
 {
 	struct usb_role_switch_desc dwc3_role_switch = {NULL};
@@ -518,6 +530,7 @@ static int dwc3_setup_role_switch(struct dwc3 *dwc)
 	dwc3_role_switch.fwnode = dev_fwnode(dwc->dev);
 	dwc3_role_switch.set = dwc3_usb_role_switch_set;
 	dwc3_role_switch.get = dwc3_usb_role_switch_get;
+	dwc3_role_switch.sync = dwc3_usb_role_switch_sync;
 	dwc3_role_switch.driver_data = dwc;
 	dwc3_role_switch.allow_userspace_control = true;
 	dwc->role_sw = usb_role_switch_register(dwc->dev, &dwc3_role_switch);
-- 
